bugs.report:
The usage line for an optional argument with a Choice type shows doubled square brackets.

```python
@click.command()
@click.argument("method", type=click.Choice(["foo", "bar", "baz"]), required=False)
def cli(method):
    pass
```

`cli --help` prints `Usage: cli [OPTIONS] [[foo|bar|baz]]` instead of `Usage: cli [OPTIONS] [foo|bar|baz]`. The same happens with `nargs=-1` and with `click.DateTime` arguments.

In a group's `--help`, the one-line help for a subcommand is cut off at abbreviations.

```python
@click.group()
def cli():
    pass

@cli.command()
def fruit():
    """Weigh apples vs. pears."""
```

`cli --help` lists `fruit  Weigh apples vs.` instead of `fruit  Weigh apples vs. pears.`. The same happens with `e.g.` or `i.e.` in the middle of a sentence. A period should only end the sentence when it ends the text or the next word starts with something other than a lowercase letter.
